@claude You created this PR and reported your findings here: https://github.com/angular-eslint/angular-eslint/issues/2425#issuecomment-2909107193 but the formatting is incorrect. Fix the formatting by running `pnpm format` and committing the result.

Additionally add a test case which covers the multiple concatenations that you spoke about. For that you simply need to use `annotatedOutputs` as an array:

Example from a different rule in the codebase:

```
convertAnnotatedSourceToFailureCase({
    description: `can remove multiple consecutive variables when fixing`,
    options: [{ allowedAliases: { $count: ['b'] } }],
    annotatedSource: `
      @for (item of items; track item.id; let a = $index, x = $even, b = $count) {,}
                                              ~~~~~~~~~~  ^^^^^^^^^
      `,
    messages: [
      {
        char: '~',
        messageId: preferContextualVariable,
        data: { name: '$index' },
      },
      {
        char: '^',
        messageId: preferContextualVariable,
        data: { name: '$even' },
      },
    ],
    annotatedOutputs: [
      `
      @for (item of items; track item.id; let x = $even, b = $count) {,}
                                                          
      `,
      `
      @for (item of items; track item.id; let b = $count) {,}
                                                          
      `,
    ],
  }),
  ```

@claude can you create a fork of this branch and submit a pull request that merges into sam/miniflare base branch that:
1. uses esbuild "context" to watch the bundle (when using esbuild to bundle a Worker with `entrypoint: string` defined and have it trigger an auto-update of the miniflare worker. This is for dev mode. It's basically hot reloading of the worker.
2. use the vite programmable API to launch the vite projects when scope.dev is true in Website? The goal is to use vite's API to start a server that hot reloads and shares the same miniflare state as the singleton miniflare instance in alchemy

I think I messed up by merging this. I thought the opacity was at the segmentation level, but it seems to be segment-specific. Could you please create a pull request to revert this change? My reasoning is that there's only one layer of opacity change at the API level, which is between Segmentations, not within them. If someone needs a different opacity for any active segment, they can use the `perSegment` configuration.

This PR also cannot get merged, https://github.com/cornerstonejs/cornerstone3D/pull/1836 as it is adding another layer of opacity configuration at api level. There is already API for perSegment configuration

